course: dictionary
lesson: 3729
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Some words have several meanings. Float is one of them. The clues in the sentence show you which meaning fits. Try each meaning in the sentence and see which one still makes sense.
explain: As a verb, to float means to stay on top of water or another liquid without sinking. It can also mean to move slowly through the air. «You smell cookies baking because tiny bits have floated through the air» uses the second meaning. The bits are moving slowly, not sitting on water.
explain: As a noun, a float is a thing that floats, such as a swimming float or a float on a fishing line. It can also be a decorated truck in a parade, or a small amount of money kept in a cash box for change. The words around it show which one you need.
fact: To float means to stay on top of water or another liquid without sinking.
fact: Wood, ice and air-filled balls float, but stones and coins sink.
fact: Salty water helps things float better.
fact: If you fall into water, you can float on your back to rest and breathe.
fact: A float can also be a decorated truck in a parade, or a small amount of money in a cash box for change.
exercise: «If a rip current carries you, you should float, signal for help or swim parallel to the shore.» What does float mean here? | To shout loudly for help | To sink slowly to the bottom | *To stay on top of the water without sinking | To swim fast straight at the shore
exercise: «You smell cookies baking because tiny bits of them have floated through the air.» What does floated mean here? | Sank to the bottom of a bowl | *Moved slowly through the air | Was cut into small pieces | Was baked in an oven
exercise: Ella holds a swimming float to learn to swim. What is a float in this sentence? | A type of fish | A small amount of money for change | *A thing that floats, used to help you stay up in the water | A decorated truck in a parade
test: «Coconuts float, and berries are eaten by birds and dropped far away.» What does float mean in this sentence? | To fall quickly onto the sand | To sink to the bottom of the sea | To move slowly through the air | *To stay on top of the water without sinking
test: Mia rode on a bright float in the Easter parade. What is a float in this sentence? | *A decorated truck in a parade | A small amount of money for change | A swimming aid for beginners | A fishing line with a bobber
exam: Which sentence uses float to mean stay on top of water? | *Wood and ice float, but stones sink. | Sam kept a float of coins in the box. | The parade float was bright red.
